<?xml version='1.0' encoding='utf-8'?>

<section xml:id="sec_nodes_topics_messages_workspace" xmlns:xi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XInclude">
  <title>Nodes, Topics, Messages, and the Workspace Environment</title>
  <introduction>
    <p>Four building blocks make up nearly every ROS2 program: nodes, topics, messages, and the workspace that ties them all together.</p>
  </introduction>

  <subsection xml:id="subsec_nodes_explained">
    <title>Nodes</title>
    <p>A <term>node</term> is a single running program that performs one logical piece of work, such as reading a sensor, running a planning algorithm, or driving a motor. Keeping each node focused on one job makes robot software easier to test, restart, and reuse across projects.</p>
  </subsection>

  <subsection xml:id="subsec_topics_explained">
    <title>Topics</title>
    <p>A <term>topic</term> is a named channel that nodes use to exchange data. A node that produces data <term>publishes</term> to a topic, and any node that needs that data <term>subscribes</term> to the same topic. Multiple nodes can publish or subscribe to the same topic without knowing about each other directly.</p>
  </subsection>

  <subsection xml:id="subsec_messages_explained">
    <title>Messages (.msg)</title>
    <p>A <term>message</term> defines the structure of data sent over a topic, similar to a struct or class definition. A <c>.msg</c> file lists field names and types, such as a <c>float64</c> for velocity or a <c>string</c> for a status label, so that publishers and subscribers agree on exactly what data is being exchanged.</p>
  </subsection>

  <subsection xml:id="subsec_workspace_explained">
    <title>The Workspace Environment</title>
    <p>A ROS2 <term>workspace</term> is the directory structure where source code, build artifacts, and installed packages live together. Building a workspace compiles nodes and message definitions and makes them available to run, which is why a newly written node typically will not be found by the system until the workspace has been built and sourced.</p>
  </subsection>
</section>
